  "hints": [
    "Choosing factors in nondecreasing order prevents permutation duplicates.",
    "At a remaining product r, try divisors d from the previous choice through sqrt(r).",
    "When d divides r, record path+[r/d], then recurse with start=d and remaining=r/d.",
    "Numbers 1 and primes produce no combinations; include composite cofactors only as part of a length-at-least-two result."
  ],
  "editorial": "Every unordered factorization has a unique nondecreasing order. At each position its next factor cannot exceed the square root of the remaining product unless it is the final cofactor, so trial division finds every branch. The independent small-domain oracle enumerates nondecreasing tuples of actual proper divisors and filters by their direct product.",
